URogue, or Ultra Rogue, appears to have been an old UNIX mutation of
Rogue, the original roguelike.  In Rogue, the Amulet of Yendor is
found on level 26, and allows passage up stairs.  URogue has many
artifacts, sprinkled through the dungeon down to level 100, any one of
which will let you upstairs.

URogue seems to be almost impossible to find these days.  There's
never been an x86 port, and source is hard to come by.  Spoilers can
be found at http://www.mit.edu/afs/athena/contrib/games/doc/urogue/urogue.doc
(browsers seem to have trouble with this link; despite the extension,
it's actually ASCII).

Reading the spoilers makes me mourn for a lost Roguelike.  It sounds
like some kind of funky, alternate-reality Nethack, with some of the
same features and ideas but implemented in different ways.

I've been playing a lot of Rogue lately, recently scoring my very
first win at a game that, by some measures, is actually harder that
Nethack.  It's interesting to go through these old games and note how
Nethack differs, and in what ways it's better and worse.  Nethack
(especially since 3.1) has since evolved into its own game.

Has anyone here ever had the opportunity to play URogue?  If so, any
stories to share?

